    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Kiana means 'where three rivers meet,' reflecting its historic river junction.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiana%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, Kiana became a major logistical hub for mine supply thanks to its river confluence.",
